\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Dismiss me not Thy service, Lord,
\par But train me for Thy will;
\par For even I, in fields so broad,
\par Some duties may fulfill
\par And I will ask for no reward,
\par Except to serve Thee still.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. How many serve, how many more 
\par May to the service come; 
\par To tend the vines, the grave to store, 
\par Thou dost appoint for some; 
\par Thou hast Thy young men at the war,
\par Thy little ones at home.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. All works are good, and each is best
\par As most it pleases Thee: 
\par Each workers pleases when the rest 
\par He serves in charity
\par And neither man nor work unblest 
\par Will Thou permit to be.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Our Master all the work hath done
\par He asks of us today;
\par Sharing His service, every one 
\par Share too His sonship may:
\par Lord, I would serve and be a son;
\par Dismiss me not, I pray.
\par 
\par   \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

